        <div class="wrapper">
            <h2 class="blueText">Macomb News</h2>
            <a class="top-right read-more" href="https://www.macomb.edu/news/index.html">Newsroom</a>
            <div class="three-column-slider row">
                                    <div class="col">
                                                                           <img alt=" Macomb Community College will host its Holiday Night Market, also known as Nattmarknad, for the second year in a row on Nov. 19, 4-9 p.m., in the Art Gallery and black box theater, L Building, at the college&#8217;s Center Campus in Clinton Township. " src="https://www.macomb.edu/news/2026/11/nightmarketgraphic.jpg"/>
                                                                                                    <h3><a href="https://www.macomb.edu/news/2026/11/news-article-holiday-night-market.html">Holiday Night Market returns on Nov. 19 to Macomb Community College </a></h3>
                                                                            <strong class="newsDate">Thursday,  November 05, 2026 9:00 AM</strong>
                                                                            <div class="content">
                               Macomb Community College will host its Holiday Night Market, also known as Nattmarknad, for the second year in a row on Nov. 19, 4-9 p.m., in the Art Gallery and black box theater, L Building, at the college&#8217;s Center Campus in Clinton Township. 
                            </div>
                                            </div>
                                    <div class="col">
                                                                           <img alt="MAP+ is an initiative designed to give students the basic skills needed to enter a construction or manufacturing career." src="https://www.macomb.edu/news/2026/10/mapplus.png"/>
                                                                                                    <h3><a href="https://www.macomb.edu/news/2026/10/michiganapprenticeshipprogram.html">Macomb Community College hosting information session on Michigan Apprenticeship Program Plus (MAP+)</a></h3>
                                                                            <strong class="newsDate">Friday,  October 30, 2026 8:30 AM</strong>
                                                                            <div class="content">
                               Macomb Community College will host an information session on the Michigan Apprenticeship Program Plus (MAP+) on Nov. 11, 5 p.m., in T Building, Room 191, on the college&#8217;s South Campus in Warren. 
                            </div>
                                            </div>
                                    <div class="col">
                                                                           <img alt="The Lorenzo Cultural Center's D&#237;a de Muertos exhibit and programming includes A Celebration of Souls: Day of the Dead in Southern Mexico, a photo exhibition featuring 26 framed color photographs. &#169; S. Vlaun" src="https://www.macomb.edu/news/2026/10/dayofthedead.png"/>
                                                                                                    <h3><a href="https://www.macomb.edu/news/2026/10/dayofthedead.html">Celebrate D&#237;a de Muertos with the Lorenzo Cultural Center through exhibit and cultural programming Oct. 19-Nov. 7</a></h3>
                                                                            <strong class="newsDate">Tuesday,  October 06, 2026 9:30 AM</strong>
                                                                            <div class="content">
                               The Lorenzo Cultural Center will host a D&#237;a de Muertos (Day of the Dead) exhibit and programming Oct. 19-Nov. 7, featuring a photo exhibition developed by the Chicago Field Museum, a Mexican film festival, workshops, a Detroit Institute of Arts excursion and cultural performances.
                            </div>
                                            </div>
                            </div>
        </div>
